        "id": 141141,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-05-06T18:47:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>arenson9 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;Arcanist Lupus wrote:<br><blockquote>That depends. &nbsp;Did you draw Rampage, Taiaha, Imbued Fire and Coolant Blast?&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nIs your point that one would do as much damage as they can to the underbosses and thugs until the other cards are drawn? Or would you focus on The Operative first? Would you try to minimize the number of villan card plays at the risk of leaving out dangerous villain and environment targets, or accept that the villain is going to get accelerated? Or is there some other strategy I'm missing?&nbsp;Don't mean to unnecessarily harp on about this. I'm looking forward to trying again when I have some time.\n</blockquote></div>\nMy point was (more or less, and admittedly cryptic) that if you don't draw the particularly strong cards, then you just play with the cards you have until you draw the strong cards or win without them.&nbsp;I realize that we've been rather unhelpful when it comes to strategies (in part, I think, because there no single 'right' way to beat the Chairman), but the post I was replying to was merely asking about likelyhood of winning, rather than how it affects your strategy, which struck me as a rather pointless hypothetical. &nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>What I'm wondering is if the scenario is winnable if you don't have one or more of some key cards early. I take it you think it is. You're probably right, but I've so far failed to prove it for myself. Admittedly, only four fails, but I've always &nbsp;found The Chairman pretty frustrating and was trying to garner some hope before trying again.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
