      {
        "id": 141144,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-05-07T00:57:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I did it. &nbsp;I beat the Chairman without ever using Brain Burn, Twist the Ether, or Savage Mana (although I had both TtE and Savage Mana in my opening hands).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I was lucky enough to have a forgiving start (Prison Break + the Fence), Rampage when I needed it, and Rook City was fairly forgiving, but it was a close game nonetheless. &nbsp;AZ bit it, and the others all reached 1 health (although Ra actually ended with 4 health thanks to his Staff).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I actually killed the Chairman first, with a Haka of Battle (nobody could possibly survive the retaliation damage, so I had to deal 24 damage in one shot), and killed the Operative with zero cards left in the villain deck.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I took quite a bit of damage keeping the doctor and the detective alive, but let me tell you - it was worth it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It was actually rather amusing though, the last turn of the game ended with two Blighted Streets and two Toxic Sludge in play - both usually undesirable cards (although Sludge can be okay), but neither of them affect you in the slightest when everybody's at 1 hp.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:18:11.498Z",
