      {
        "id": 141147,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-05-08T21:21:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>FINALLY won this.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A relativley early Twist the Ether on The Operative allowed Absolute Zero to tank and gave me time to find Savage Mana and start eating the Thugs. I meant to take out The Operative before putting a third Underboss in the trash, but Rook City jumped the gun on me. I eventually unloaded Savage Mana, combined with a Haka of Battle, to one-shot The Chairman and in the process was able to funnel half of The Operative's retaliatory attacks as fire on Absolute Zero through the Isothermic Transducer, turning them into attacks on The Operative.</p><p>Even so, the next villain turn &nbsp;lead to three underbosses coming out and&nbsp;<span>wiped out everyone but Absolute Zero.</span></p><p><span>By that time, though, Absolute Zero had a whole bunch of cards in play and it a Hoarfire and his base power via Isothermic Transducer was enough to finish The Operative.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think part of why I've had trouble with this scenario is that when playing the video game version, I get impatient with doing things like seeing how many cards are left in a deck or exactly which cards are in a trash pile. I got surprised a number of times by which cards were coming up to play or when a trash was shuffled back in to a deck.</p>",
